  "text": " tasked with deriving the required relationship.\n\n.FlatAppearance:\". ف\nLet us start by determining which of the given equations will have the common root. Since $b$ and $c$ are positive, the common root should be positive as well. \n\nSince the common root is positive, and $c$ is positive, the common root can either be the positive or negative root of the quadratic equation $x^2 - 8x + 16 = 0$. Let's solve this equation for $x$.\n\n$$x = \\frac{8 \\pm \\sqrt{8^2-4 \\cdot 16}}{2} = 4$$\n\nSo, $x = 4$ or $x = -4$ are the possible roots. Since $x$ is positive, the common root is $x = 4$.\n\nSubstitute the values of $x$ and $c$ into the equation $x^2 + bx + c = 0$ to determine the values of $b$ and $c$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{align}\nx^2 + bx + c & = 0 \\\\\n4^2 + b \\cdot 4 + c & = 0 \\\\\n16 + 4b + c & = 0 \\\\\n4b + c & = -16 &\n\\end{align}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the values of $x$ and $c$ into the equation $y^2 - cy + 4 = 0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{align}\ny^2 - cy + 4 & = 0 \\\\\n4^2 - c \\cdot 4 + 4 & = 0 \\\\\n16 - 4c + 4 & = 0 \\\\\n16 - 4c & = -4 \\\\\n-4c & = -20 \\\\\nc & = 5 &\n\\end{align}\n$$\n\nSo, the largest possible value for $c$ satisfying the condition $c = \\frac{c^2 - 16}{8b}$ is $c = 5$.",
